{{ '**Away** - safety band only' if away else ('**Night** targets' if night else '**Day** targets') }} · outdoor {{ '-' if o <= -900 else (o | round(1) ~ '°') }}{% if o > -900 %} ({{ 'terrace' if has_value('sensor.outdoor_motion_temperature') else 'forecast' }}){% endif %} · heat below {{ hbo }}° / cool above {{ cao }}°{% set rz = [('climate.livingroom_thermostat_livingroom_thermostat'),('climate.bedroom_trv_bedroom_trv'),('climate.kid1_room_trv_kid1_room_trv'),('climate.kid2_room_trv_kid2_room_trv')] %}{% set heating = rz | select('is_state_attr', 'hvac_action', 'heating') | list | count %}{% set ph = ['living_room','office','bedroom','kid1','kid2'] | map('regex_replace', '^', 'input_boolean.climate_preheat_') | select('is_state', 'on') | list | count %}

Radiators: {{ 'follow the room targets' if is_state('automation.climate_radiators','on') else '**on Tado schedules** (automation off)' }}{{ (' · ' ~ heating ~ ' heating now') if heating else '' }} · morning warm-up {{ ('in ' ~ ph ~ ' room' ~ ('' if ph == 1 else 's')) if ph else 'off' }}{% if is_state('input_boolean.climate_auto','off') %}

⚠️ **Automation is OFF**{% set nsf = namespace(fon=[]) %}{% for n, s in [('Living room','living_room'),('Office','office'),('Bedroom','bedroom'),('Kids room 1','kid1'),('Kids room 2','kid2')] %}{% if is_state('input_boolean.climate_air_filter_' ~ s,'on') %}{% set nsf.fon = nsf.fon + [n] %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% if nsf.fon %} · **Air filter idle: {{ nsf.fon | join(', ') }}**{% endif %}{% if is_state('input_boolean.climate_safety_always','on') %} · safety limits still apply{% endif %}{% endif %}

<details><summary><ha-icon icon="mdi:information-outline"></ha-icon></summary>

**House mode** follows the outdoor temperature: below *heat below* the house heats, above *cool above* it cools. In between (shoulder) nothing heats or cools, and rooms with **Air filter** on run the fan only.

**Night** targets apply while the alarm is armed for the night. **Away**: after 30 minutes armed away only the safety band is kept.

**Radiators** follow the room targets while the radiator automation is on, otherwise the Tado schedules. **Morning warm-up** heats early so a room is at its day target when the night ends.

The line below the switches flags: a room with no temperature reading (its safety band cannot be checked) · implausible sensor calibration (those probes are ignored for their backups) · a radiator valve above its room target (boiler and AC take turns) · a stale restart stamp (a person at the wall can no longer be told from a faulty unit) · a unit not responding (comfort throttled, safety still runs) · a manual hold (the automation hands off until it expires) · an inverted house band (all comfort control stands down) · safety limits off (no frost protection, no away band).

The gear opens the advanced settings.

</details>
